You are completely right. When modifying React JSX, changing an implicit return ( to an explicit block { return ( or wrapping components in a new <Tooltip> is notorious for breaking the closing brackets at the bottom.
If patching it line-by-line is breaking the brackets, the fastest way to fix this without syntax errors is to replace the whole blocks.
Here is exactly how to fix the brackets for those two steps:
### Fix for Step 4 (The Map Loop Brackets)
Because we changed rows.map((row) => ( to rows.map((row) => { return (, you have to close the new { at the very end of the row loop.
Scroll all the way down to where the row map ends (right before the Add Row button).
**Find this exact code at the bottom of the loop:**
```javascript
              {index < rows.length - 1 && (
                <Box
                  sx={{
                    borderBottom: 1,
                    borderColor: "divider",
                    my: 2,
                  }}
                />
              )}
            </React.Fragment>
          ))}

```
**Replace it with this (notice the added ); and the }):**
```javascript
              {index < rows.length - 1 && (
                <Box
                  sx={{
                    borderBottom: 1,
                    borderColor: "divider",
                    my: 2,
                  }}
                />
              )}
            </React.Fragment>
          );
          })}

```
### Fix for Step 6 (The CGL Tooltip Brackets)
